# Provisioning runs on Debian — shell scripts/templates MUST be LF (CRLF breaks the
# shebang and `set` parsing). The repo's core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite them.
provisioning/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
# The repo standardizes on LF everywhere (the index is already all-LF; idiomatic for OSS, and
# PowerShell 5.1 + the n8n tooling all read LF fine). Explicit per-type rules so the convention
# survives a fresh clone regardless of core.autocrlf. Encoding (UTF-8 / BOM for *.ps1) is governed
# by .editorconfig, not here — git does not touch the byte-order mark.
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.psd1 text eol=lf
# tests/mock_telegram/server.js runs under Node IN the Debian test container — keep LF like the rest.
*.js   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonc text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.tpl  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf
# Extensionless Dockerfile (test-substrate base image, built on Linux) — keep LF like the rest of the tree.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
# Extensionless GitHub meta files (CODEOWNERS) — keep LF like the rest of the tree.
.github/CODEOWNERS text eol=lf
# Extensionless linter config (shellcheck rc) — keep LF like the rest of the tree.
config/shellcheckrc text eol=lf
# Dotfile-named linter config (sqlfluff) — no extension `*.sqlfluff` rule would match `.sqlfluff`.
config/.sqlfluff text eol=lf
# Showcase-Site (docs/site): Hugo emits LF; without explicit rules core.autocrlf=true would check
# out CRLF and permanently break the build_site.ps1 -Verify regen-diff (Site-Phase 2026-07-02).
*.html text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.svg  text eol=lf
# Binaere Test-Dokumente (tests/mock_telegram/docs): ein PDF traegt Byte-Offsets (xref) -> nie Zeilenenden umschreiben.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
# Release-Signierschluessel (provisioning/keys, OpenPGP binaer): die provisioning/**-Zeile oben darf ihn nie als Text
# normalisieren, sonst passt der Bund nicht mehr zu RELEASE_KEY_B64 in install.sh (contract_lint 24).
*.gpg binary
*.sig binary
